{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>A light.</b> Some say a window; some say a precious stone that illuminated for them (Bereshit Rabbah there)." "<b>And to a cubit you shall finish it from above.</b> Its roof is sloped and rises until it narrows from above and stands at a cubit, so that the waters would flow down from here and from there." "<b>You shall set it on its side.</b> So that the rains would not fall into it." "<b>With lower, second, and third stories.</b> Three stories, one atop the other — the upper for the people, the middle for living quarters, the lower for the waste (there)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:46.536810167Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}